WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.780
We have a constantly growing population.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:10.769
This means we will need 50% to 70% more food by 2050.

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:17.440
So where are we going to find 50% to 70% more food
in only 30 years?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.834
Nature is already building
and sustaining all life on Earth.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:26.920
We don't have to reinvent the wheel,
the calories we need

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.961
and we eat and we uptake from food
comes from the sun

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.020
The starting point for all food on Earth is
photosynthesis.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.380
Sunlight combines with carbon dioxide and
water in plants and forms oxygen and glucose.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.340
This sugar is stored in fruits, roots and
vegetables.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.680
One startup in London thinks harnessing photosynthesis

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.240
in microscopic plants could go some way to

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.600
solving our planet's imminent food crisis.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.160
We have to start with a microalgae strain

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.040
They are the fastest-growing, photosynthesizing
organism on this planet.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.580
These very tiny microscopic plants 
contain hundreds and hundreds

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.540
of very precious, healthy food molecules

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:22.140
that can be extracted and utilized in our own food.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.940
Microalgaes aren't on many menus yet but
they might be the new superfoods

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.520
packed full of vitamins, antioxidants and minerals
they sustain trillions of animals on our planet.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.400
Arborea claims its technology - 
the BioSolar Leaf - helps grow this food

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.360
at rates rarely seen in nature.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.780
Arborea's BioSolar Leaf looks similar to a solar panel

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.800
It's a technology that
can produce and can grow

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:57.368
hundreds of different microscopic plants to
produce hundreds of different ingredients.

00:01:57.368 --> 00:02:02.540
It enables to grow them very quickly
but also in a very efficient way

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.320
therefore consuming a very little amount of energy

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:11.380
We can produce a lot of protein in a very
small surface area. Imagine that we can produce

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:18.060
more protein for a defined surface area than
any other plant-based or animal-based

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.200
source on this planet by orders of magnitude.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.400
We harvest some of this liquid,

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.800
we separate the liquid from the microalgae
and then we dry it and usually it's either

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:36.301
in a flake form or a powder form, ready to
be shipped to food producers

00:02:36.301 --> 00:02:41.212
so they can utilize them in all sorts of
food products they want.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.920
Arborea imagines their food being used as
a supplement,

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.260
or being sold on its own in stores.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.660
There are hundreds of thousands of species
of microalgae, all with different qualities,

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:59.240
flavors and even colors - something that
could be interesting to food producers.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.840
What we can do with these ingredients
that we extract from this microalgae

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.120
is that we can utilize them for
all sorts of processed food.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:14.020
It's not only replacing a synthetic or
unsustainable food ingredients

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.160
But it's also adding health benefits,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.100
active health benefits to our processed food.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.700
Let's say that we have Arborea's 'Big Blue'
together with a yogurt.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:30.060
This yogurt might contain more antioxidant
than you find in an apple.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.360
Originally blue was associated with something synthetic,

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.940
something unhealthy, right?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:40.168
Maybe blue is going to become the new color
associated with health, why not?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.900
Arborea's powdered food might not look all
that appetizing,

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.180
but their intention is substance over style.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.060
Feeding our growing population with the right
things, in a better way

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.960
might improve our chances of future food security.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:03.180
I strongly believe that if we as humans
can harness photosynthesis

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.040
then we have high chances to help
solve the issues that we are facing today

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.300
and that we will face in the future.

